{%- comment -%}
  theinmag-stockist-gate

  Entry lightbox for the stockist picker on /pages/instock. Rendered ONCE,
  only when theinmag-shop-grid has stockist_pricing on, so it can never
  appear on /pages/shop.

  Two ways past, deliberately unequal in weight: enter a stockist code (the
  yellow stamp, the action we want) or carry on at retail (a plain text
  button). Nobody is trapped, but the decision is explicit, which is the
  whole point: today a stockist lands on a page of retail prices with no
  idea those are not their prices.

  A mINion from the sitewide pool peeks over the top edge of the card and
  can be switched, exactly as on the 404 page. The pool snippet is rendered
  by the section; the switch button reuses the pool's own sessionStorage
  cache of valid indices, so it never probes twice.

  Archetype: design system 6.4, hero choice gate (decision-first), which
  names a future stockist page as its use case. Mechanics are lifted from
  the peek lightbox already on this page: the module moves this node to
  <body> so position:fixed resolves against the viewport rather than a
  transformed section ancestor, ESC closes, focus is trapped while open and
  returns to the trigger on close.

  Behaviour lives in assets/theinmag-stockist-pricing.js. This file is
  markup only.

  Params:
    gate_heading  - string, the question
    gate_body     - string, the one-line explainer
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign gate_heading = gate_heading | default: 'Ordering for your shop?'
  assign gate_body = gate_body | default: "Pop your code in and you'll see your real prices."
-%}

<div class="theinmag-stockist-gate" data-stockist-gate hidden>
  <div class="theinmag-stockist-gate__scrim"></div>
  <div
    class="theinmag-stockist-gate__card"
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-labelledby="theinmag-stockist-gate-title"
  >
    <div class="theinmag-stockist-gate__stage" data-stockist-character-stage>
      <span class="theinmag-stockist-gate__character" data-theinmag-pool-character data-stockist-character></span>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Sits in the card's top right corner, beside the character it swaps.
      Icon only: the label is for screen readers and the hover tooltip, so
      the card stays minimal.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="theinmag-stockist-gate__switch"
      data-stockist-character-switch
      title="Switch mINion"
      aria-label="Switch to a different character"
    >
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M3 12a9 9 0 0 1 15.5-6.3M21 6v5h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M21 12a9 9 0 0 1-15.5 6.3M3 18v-5h5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>
    </button>

    <h2 class="theinmag-stockist-gate__title" id="theinmag-stockist-gate-title">{{ gate_heading }}</h2>
    <p class="theinmag-stockist-gate__body">{{ gate_body }}</p>

    <div class="theinmag-stockist-gate__form">
      <span class="theinmag-stockist-field" data-stockist-field>
        <input
          type="text"
          class="theinmag-stockist-field__input"
          data-stockist-code-input
          placeholder="Your stockist code"
          aria-label="Your stockist code"
          autocomplete="off"
          autocapitalize="characters"
          autocorrect="off"
          spellcheck="false"
          enterkeyhint="go"
        >
        <button type="button" class="theinmag-stockist-field__submit" data-stockist-submit>See my prices</button>
      </span>
      <p class="theinmag-stockist-status" data-stockist-status role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Outlined purple, the sitewide secondary button. Yellow stays on the
      one action we actually want, per design system 7.5 Q22.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button type="button" class="theinmag-stockist-gate__browse" data-stockist-gate-close data-stockist-browse>
      I'm curious - just having a look
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
